===== RTL REPAIR DECISION =====
schema_version: '1.0'
action: repair
root_cause: "The SHA-256 round-constant table K is malformed in rtl.sv: the declaration\
  \ `localparam logic [31:0] K [0:63]` requires 64 initializers, but the assignment-pattern\
  \ body (lines 10-27) supplies only 62 constants. Indices 62 and 63 are left uninitialized,\
  \ so Verilator rejects the RTL at elaboration with 'Assignment pattern missed initializing\
  \ elements: 62/63', which aborts the build for every test before any simulation\
  \ runs. The list is additionally corrupted against the FIPS 180-4 constants mandated\
  \ by specification.md \xA73: index 10 is 243185bf (should be 243185be), index 31\
  \ is 14292977 (should be 14292967), and constants 2e1b2138 (K[33]) and 4d2c6dfc\
  \ (K[34]) are deleted, shifting all indices \u226533 down by two."
evidence:
- 'simulation_result.json: all 11 tests (Sha256ResetInitializationTest ... Sha256RandomizedTest)
  report status=runtime_error, category=runtime_error, returncode=2, results_file_exists=false,
  and every log shows the identical Verilator build failure: ''%Error: .../sha256.sv:10:40:
  Assignment pattern missed initializing elements: 62'' and '': 63'', then ''%Error:
  Exiting due to 2 error(s)'' followed by `make: *** ... Vtop.mk Error 1`. Scoreboard/assertion
  counts are all 0 because the DUT never compiled.'
- 'Source grounding: the RTL under analysis (rtl.sv, byte-identical to the simulated
  /rtl_verification/accepted/sha256.sv, confirmed by diff) declares an unpacked array
  `logic [31:0] K [0:63]` (64 elements) yet the initializer body (lines 11-26) contains
  exactly 62 `32''h...` literals (counted). Verilator 5.042 (as captured in the log)
  requires every element of an assignment pattern to be initialized when the array
  has no default, producing errors for K[62] and K[63].'
- "Spec grounding: specification.md \xA73.2 requires 'The 64 SHA-256 round constants\
  \ K[0..63]' per FIPS 180-4. Comparing the 62 present RTL constants against the FIPS\
  \ 180-4 table shows the only in-list diffs are K[10] 243185bf vs 243185be and K[31]\
  \ 14292977 vs 14292967, and that 2e1b2138/4d2c6dfc (K[33]/K[34]) are absent with\
  \ the tail shifted, so appending two arbitrary values would compile but leave every\
  \ K[\u226533] wrong; restoring the full standard table is required for intended\
  \ behavior."
- 'TB/infrastructure not implicated: the failing step is Verilator elaborating the
  DUT source itself (note: In instance ''sha256''); the cocotb/pyuvm harness, Makefile,
  and verilator flags never execute. This is an RTL defect (defective constant declaration),
