===== RTL REPAIR DECISION =====
schema_version: '1.0'
action: repair
root_cause: 'The DUT still honors a start-while-busy by restarting the in-flight transaction:
  rtl.sv line 128 uses an un-gated `if (start)`, taking priority over the `else if
  (busy)` processing branch. The frozen TB grades completion by a fixed-cycle window
  per start edge (transaction_completes_within_latency requires digest != 0 within
  [start+64 .. start+70]). Sha256StartWhileBusyRestartsSequence re-asserts start with
  a different block 10 cycles into the first transaction (RESTART_DELAY_CYCLES=10);
  the restart aborts the "abc" computation and the restarted empty-message computation
  only writes digest at start2+64 (> start1+70), so the first start''s digest is still
  0x0 at cycle 76. This trips the assertion (''transaction started at cycle 5 did
  not produce a non-zero digest within 64..70 cycles (digest still 0x0 at cycle 76)'')
  and produces the scoreboard DIGEST MISMATCH for txn_id=1 with actual_digest=0x0.
  specification.md section 5 defines intended behavior: ''A transaction begins when
  start == 1 && DUT is idle'', and the verification plan discrepancy DISC-017 (start
  not gated by busy) records the exact recommended fix ''if (start && !busy)''. Gating
  start on !busy makes the first transaction complete normally (abc digest inside
  its valid window), and since digest mismatches are catch reports (not test failures),
  the StartWhileBusyRestarts test passes. The other currently-failing test (Sha256RandomizedTest)
  is NOT RTL-caused: the 2 INVALID BLOCK reports (txn 4, 12) come from the frozen
  golden reference''s block_to_digest() using block.index(b''\x80'') to find the padding
  marker, so canonical one-block paddings whose random message (bytes 0..255) contains
  an 0x80 byte are mis-rejected -- verified txn_id=12''s DUT digest 0x442e6052...
  equals hashlib.sha256(true_message), i.e., the RTL datapath is correct and only
  the TB reference-model validator cannot grade it; no RTL change can fix that. The
  two digest=0 scoreboard mismatches (txn 17/18) are the plan''s intended reset_during_processing
  (p=0.1) injections aborting transactions (mismatch catch reports, not failures).'
evidence:
- 'simulation_result.json (authoritative) + tb/.chia_sim/Sha256StartWhileBusyRestartsTest.xml:
  test status=runtime_error, failure=''transaction_completes_within_latency violated:
  transaction started at cycle 5 did not produce a non-zero digest within 64..70 cycles
  (digest still 0x0000...0000 at cycle 76)''; scoreboard log shows ''DIGEST MISMATCH
  txn_id=1: block=0x6162638000... actual_digest=0x0000...0000 cycle_of_mismatch=79
  (sampled 70 cycles after start edge)''.'
- 'Sequence timing (sha256_sequences.py Sha256StartWhileBusyRestartsSequence): first
  start (abc) -> wait 1 -> wait RESTART_DELAY_CYCLES=10 -> second start (empty) while
  DUT is still processing. With line 128 `if (start)` un-gated, the second edge restarts
  the DUT, so the first start''s digest can never appear in its [start+64, start+70]
  band.'
- 'specification.md section 5: ''A transaction begins when: start == 1 && DUT is idle''
  -- the intended behavior is to ignore start while busy; verification_plan.yaml DISC-017
  (rtl: ''if (start) executes regardless of busy state'') documents the deviation
  and recommends ''Gate start with !busy: if (start && !busy)''.'
- 'Datapath correctness is independent of this failure: 9/11 tests pass; directed
  KATs match the golden reference (Sha256AbcMessageTest MATCH digest=0xba7816bf8f01cfea414140de5dae2223b00361a396177a9cb410ff61f20015ad
  at cycle 79); Sha256RandomizedTest matched 16/20 digests.'
- 'Sha256RandomizedTest failure is TB/reference-model, not RTL: both INVALID BLOCK
  reports (''Invalid length field in padded block.'', txn 4 and 12) are canonical
  one-block paddings whose messages contain byte 0x80; reference_model.py block_to_digest
  finds the bogus marker with block.index(b''\x80''). Independent check: txn_id=12''s
  observed DUT digest 0x442e6052b83b029191a7c525b5af30936ad7ad3def210d7ddfe68081351aba29
  equals hashlib.sha256(block[:32]).hexdigest(), proving the RTL computed the correct
  digest and only the TB''s padding validator is at fault. The DIGEST MISMATCH txn
  17/18 (actual=0) correspond to the plan''s reset_during_processing injections aborting
  in-flight transactions -- intended catch reports, not failures.'
- 'The start-gating repair preserves all currently passing tests: back_to_back and
  randomized back-to-back starts occur >=70 cycles after the prior start (DUT idle
  after start+65), corner reset_during_processing clears latency windows on reset,
  and the retained done<=1''b1 reset/default behavior (required by Sha256ResetInitializationTest,
  reset_sets_done_high, done_behavior_continuous) is untouched.'
confidence: high
changes:
- file: rtl.sv
  action: modify
  instructions:
  - 'Gate transaction acceptance on the DUT being idle: change line 128 `if (start)
    begin` to `if (start && !busy) begin` (matches specification.md section 5 ''start
    == 1 && DUT is idle'' and verification-plan DISC-017''s recorded recommendation).
    This makes a start-while-busy be ignored instead of aborting/restarting the in-flight
    transaction, so every accepted start completes its 64-round compression within
    the frozen TB''s fixed [start+64, start+70] latency window.'
  - 'Do not modify anything else: keep `done <= 1''b1` on reset (line 100) and the
    default `done <= 1''b1` (line 126), keep the datapath (K/W/Ch/Maj/sigma/T1/T2/state/feed-forward,
    round 0..63 with `round == 63` completion), and leave `busy <= 1''b0` at completion
    -- the frozen TB codifies done==1 continuity and start-while-busy is the only
    remaining RTL-caused failure in this iteration.'
  - 'Note: the Sha256RandomizedTest failure (invalid_block_count=2 from reference-model
    rejection of 0x80-containing messages) is a frozen-TB/reference-model limitation
    and is not addressable by any RTL change; it should be handled in a later stage
    (template_bug/no_repair), not by rtl.sv edits.'

